1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=\\frac{11}{2}$ and the vertical radius has length $b=\\frac{3}{2}.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{(\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{(\\frac{3}{2})}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\frac{121}{4})}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\frac{9}{4})} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{4{x}^{2}}{121}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{9} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-279126/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f88c1deb-cd11-5b68-b90b-2d8edfae2469"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-279126"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-69891/selection/600371ddd5b2587dbf30c7783e62d5ac5d0d8d02c57937c88c59ddb5401a058e" :answer/id #uuid "0e30b6dc-9b27-56f4-bac6-239acae40580" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{1}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69891/selection/edba392f0114807cac3dc6a4ac9e721cf525c8f72ca3b84fc846a68488312157" :answer/id #uuid "1e277316-bfd8-578b-903a-06f63e69e1a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{1}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69891/selection/537f321e6f52ce8cbd25a14d43ecc5e372007059dc8fc3b789ef45bc08a8d925" :answer/id #uuid "1ac19654-e9cf-5cbc-ad79-5e17c5cf6676" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{1}=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-69891/selection/aeca7b7d0e65453c9cdc69f581959c5f4605f44f4db814fe38dfddbee99ef7c8" :answer/id #uuid "384e03ef-b31d-57fa-a817-8e57e5fc9381" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\