swer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-279158/field-1/4abb08e1747f947b402b1b7cb8617aeb1706107c2d769df54673d54a8fa73f49" :answer-field/choices ["q-279158/field-1/4abb08e1747f947b402b1b7cb8617aeb1706107c2d769df54673d54a8fa73f49"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-279158" :question/id #uuid "1fa0f7da-6dac-5383-8bb1-c2e631b620a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-279158" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13957964/assets/c583eabd1719e94dc727b876b944c839a39124adb341d88357cf954dbed79646.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=\\frac{9}{2}$ and the vertical radius has length $b=\\frac{13}{2}.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{(\\frac{9}{2})}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{(\\frac{13}{2})}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\frac{81}{4})}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\frac{169}{4})} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{4{x}^{2}}{81}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{169} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-279158/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "de557d1d-5f27-50e3-bcba-22b21f83267f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-279158"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-16454/selection/6755c9fb04cdbc4cdbf5391f31f83f87fc1a2d418bd08d243f11c85fb59bdd7d" :answer/id #uuid "967eea40-f5c2-5dc8-8973-b6d75547cb4d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$4\\sqrt{3}$ and $2\\sqrt{3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16454/selection/ec1fa8e706569b98ebb2fc8eb40d71764294e87cce55d22674e5c