at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=3$ and ${b}^{2}=12.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=3,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{3}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=12,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{12}=2\\sqrt{3}.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $b=2\\sqrt{3},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=\\sqrt{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3}=4\\sqrt{3},$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot \\sqrt{3}=2\\sqrt{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-16454/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-16454"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-7596/selection/40148c9d7ac7b6262b45f56e187242cedf0c466f8f8f43dbe9f8d735919ed2b0" :answer/id #uuid "dc8ae039-2e0c-5b27-928b-48dca10ec333" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$3\\sqrt{2}$ and $3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7596/selection/03b9d70ffca29267772c5c89ef9afbae091da50fa5e35c66893876411122ed3d" :answer/id #uuid "cfe58789-fd77-57f3-bbce-f97e5dd67d1a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$6\\sqrt{2}$ and $3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7596/selection/96fc253e0c66345f8ca564a17c0c1fae992c5ec5b278e6bbbdeea53d550648cd" :answer/id #uuid "fc5b7510-1302-5aca-a005-6b58e2a7e35e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$18$ and $9$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7596/selection/c699f2ff3c9baae9ac49bf2286be75cce58afc93074ffbac97c38b57ea33060a" :answer/id #uuid "dafdf6e3-8816-5d7a-9aae-28d3972e49d6" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$6\\sqrt{2}$ and $6$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-7596/selection/5fd750aaa374560dd76ad0a7b30c83e276a4ec78a7dfea009715277281